# Build context filter. Docker sends everything in the project directory to
# the daemon unless matched here. The daemon then hashes files during COPY
# to compute cache keys — and if a hashed file is a broken symlink, the COPY
# fails with "failed to compute cache key".
#
# node_modules is the primary offender. It is reinstalled inside the image
# by the deps stage (`npm ci`), so there is zero reason to send it across.
# It also contains workspace symlinks that can point to moved/deleted paths,
# which is exactly the failure we are fixing here.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in the image
**/node_modules

# Build outputs
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Env files — never bake secrets into images
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local dev artifacts
**/.pgdata
**/.cert
*.log
coverage

# Git history — irrelevant for build, and .git can contain refs to
# unreachable objects (e.g. after gc or after a partial clone) that break
# BuildKit's hashing
.git
.gitignore

# Editors
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode

# Docs and screenshots
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Test artifacts
apps/api/test-results